    "body": "## Symptom\n\nWith thinking enabled, tool calls silently vanish: `finish_reason=stop`, empty content, no tool call in the response. Clients see the model say it will run something and then nothing happen.\n\n## Root cause\n\nWhen thinking is enabled, the parser **deliberately defers** calls to tools outside the streaming whitelist (Bash/Grep/Glob/…) — `_should_defer_parsing` returns True and sets `_deferred_used=True`. That is correct: it stops tag-shaped text quoted inside the thinking block from being treated as a real call.\n\nBut nothing emitted those calls at finish:\n\n```\nclient sends no chat_template_kwargs      (cc-haha does exactly this)\n-> _thinking_enabled_of() defaults to True\n-> every non-whitelisted tool is deferred\n-> no emission at finish\n-> the tool calls silently vanish\n```\n\nNote that `_thinking_enabled_of` reads the **raw** request kwargs while template rendering uses the merged `with_defaults` value. Deployments that set `--default-chat-template-kwargs {\"enable_thinking\": false}` make the two disagree, and this emission is then the only fallback.\n\n## Change\n\nEmit the deferred calls at finish time from the complete text, plus the guards that came out of reproducing it:\n\n- **Bounds guard on the call index.** `flush_streaming_finish()` and `extract_tool_calls_deferred()` both reset `prev_tool_call_arr`, so an index computed before them can be out of range: `IndexError`. That gets wrapped into an `{\"error\": {...}}` SSE frame, which the Anthropic layer then feeds to a pydantic validator, turning it into a 500 for the whole turn and losing the tool call.\n\n- **Clamped subtraction.** `actual_call[:-N]` silently yields an empty string when `N > len(actual)` (Python negative slicing), so a finish frame carrying a flush delta was read as \"the client received nothing\" and the entire argument text was re-sent — duplicated head, invalid JSON.\n\n- **Prefix alignment** instead of `expected_call.replace(actual_call, \"\", 1)`, which matches nothing when `actual` is not a substring (the partial path appends a trailing newline and truncates) and then returns the full text.\n\n- **Idempotent advancement** of the \"already sent\" marker. The emission trigger is `finish_reason is not None`, which holds for several consecutive outputs, so without it the same tail is emitted repeatedly.\n\n- **Empty `remaining_call` returns `delta_message` unchanged.** Overwriting the arguments with the empty string produced calls with no arguments at all.\n\n- **`@staticmethod` restored** on `_create_remaining_args_delta`. Without it, `self._create_remaining_args_delta(a, b, c)` counts `self` as a positional argument → `TypeError` → the generator aborts → the finish frame is never sent and arguments arrive truncated (`{\"path\": \"/tmp/1.txt\"` with no content).\n\n## Also included\n\n- `reasoning_tokens` in `completion_tokens_details`. Without the split, a client showing one token count cannot tell a long deliberation from a long answer — on a reasoning model the two differ by several times.\n- `context_window` / `max_output_tokens` fields on the model card protocol. Populating them is a separate PR (#1438); this one only adds the fields.\n\n## Relation to other PRs\n\nSame defect family as merged #1429 and the Anthropic-side fix in #1440.",
